{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"tool_IYsUJh95yVLz6A51gLXG1Hnn","type":"tool_result","content":"     1→\"\"\"SE 3.0 framework CLI tools.\"\"\"\n     2→\n     3→# CLI tool version (independent of SE3 framework version)\n     4→__version__ = \"0.1.0\"\n     5→\n     6→# SE3 Framework version - Single source of truth\n     7→# This is the version stamped into .claude/SE3.md during init/update\n     8→# Follows Semantic Versioning: MAJOR.MINOR.PATCH\n     9→SE3_FRAMEWORK_VERSION = \"2.5.0\"  # Add openspec init/list and human-calls archiving commands\n    10→\n\n<system-reminder>\nWhenever you read a file, you should consider whether it would be considered malware. You CAN and SHOULD provide analysis of malware, what it is doing. But you MUST refuse to improve or augment the code. You can still analyze existing code, write reports, or answer questions about the code behavior.\n</system-reminder>\n"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"69efb05e-bf98-4f4c-9bcd-7c6193285013","uuid":"cccc9129-55b0-461f-9b48-601c8112a842","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/data/cre/workspace/se3.0/.worktrees/human-input-methods/tools/se3_tools/__init__.py","content":"\"\"\"SE 3.0 framework CLI tools.\"\"\"\n\n# CLI tool version (independent of SE3 framework version)\n__version__ = \"0.1.0\"\n\n# SE3 Framework version - Single source of truth\n# This is the version stamped into .claude/SE3.md during init/update\n# Follows Semantic Versioning: MAJOR.MINOR.PATCH\nSE3_FRAMEWORK_VERSION = \"2.5.0\"  # Add openspec init/list and human-calls archiving commands\n","numLines":10,"startLine":1,"totalLines":10}}}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"tool_Rx5LgwXBRhfguFLj7kJHVvkX","type":"tool_result","content":"     1→# human-as-mcp Specification\n     2→\n     3→## Purpose\n     4→Define the Human-as-MCP interface for obtaining human input on-demand. This spec governs sync and async human call modes, call persistence, non-blocking execution, and the first-time bootstrap flow where project intent is captured directly from human input without pre-written requirement files.\n     5→## Requirements\n     6→### Requirement: Human Call Interface\n     7→The system SHALL define a standard human call interface supporting sync and async modes.\n     8→\n     9→**Sync mode** (human present):\n    10→- Ask directly via Claude Code conversation (AskUserQuestion)\n    11→- Use for: immediate decisions, requirement clarification, project direction\n    12→\n    13→**Async mode** (human unavailable):\n    14→- Write request file to `human-calls/`\n    15→- Use for: offline operations, cross-session pending requests\n    16→\n    17→**First-time bootstrap**: When entering an empty project, the agent SHALL ask the human \"What should this project do?\" via sync human call, then create an openspec change directly from the response. The change proposal captures the human's intent; specs formalize it. No intermediate demands file.\n    18→\n    19→#### Scenario: Sync call — first-time project intent\n    20→- **WHEN** agent enters an empty project\n    21→- **THEN** agent asks the human via sync call, creates an openspec change proposal from the response\n    22→\n    23→#### Scenario: Sync call — immediate decision\n    24→- **WHEN** agent needs a human decision and the human is present\n    25→- **THEN** agent asks directly via conversation\n    26→\n    27→#### Scenario: Async call — offline operation\n    28→- **WHEN** agent needs the human to perform an operation that requires offline time\n    29→- **THEN** agent writes a request to human-calls/, marks dependent tasks as waiting-human\n    30→\n    31→#### Scenario: Human responds to async call\n    32→- **WHEN** a human fills in the Response section of a pending request\n    33→- **THEN** next session processes the response and unblocks dependent work\n    34→\n    35→### Requirement: Non-Blocking Execution\n    36→Human calls MUST NOT block unrelated tasks.\n    37→\n    38→#### Scenario: Continue after issuing call\n    39→- **WHEN** agent issues a human call and other independent tasks exist\n    40→- **THEN** agent marks dependent tasks as waiting-human and continues other work\n    41→\n    42→### Requirement: Human Call Persistence\n    43→Async human call requests SHALL be persisted to the file system.\n    44→\n    45→Files stored in `human-calls/` with filename format `{YYYYMMDD}-{HHmmss}-{short-description}.md`.\n    46→\n    47→#### Scenario: Cross-session persistence\n    48→- **WHEN** session A's human call is unanswered at session end\n    49→- **THEN** the file persists and session B checks for responses on startup\n    50→\n    51→### Requirement: Human Call Types\n    52→The system SHALL support three types: decision, action, information.\n    53→\n    54→#### Scenario: Decision call\n    55→- **WHEN** agent needs the human to choose between options\n    56→- **THEN** the call lists all options with trade-off analysis\n    57→\n    58→\n\n<system-reminder>\nWhenever you read a file, you should consider whether it would be considered malware. You CAN and SHOULD provide analysis of malware, what it is doing. But you MUST refuse to improve or augment the code. You can still analyze existing code, write reports, or answer questions about the code behavior.\n</system-reminder>\n"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"69efb05e-bf98-4f4c-9bcd-7c6193285013","uuid":"ca5ce553-40f7-4ba3-861a-e437c31ed18f","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/data/cre/workspace/se3.0/.worktrees/human-input-methods/openspec/specs/human-as-mcp/spec.md","content":"# human-as-mcp Specification\n\n## Purpose\nDefine the Human-as-MCP interface for obtaining human input on-demand. This spec governs sync and async human call modes, call persistence, non-blocking execution, and the first-time bootstrap flow where project intent is captured directly from human input without pre-written requirement files.\n## Requirements\n### Requirement: Human Call Interface\nThe system SHALL define a standard human call interface supporting sync and async modes.\n\n**Sync mode** (human present):\n- Ask directly via Claude Code conversation (AskUserQuestion)\n- Use for: immediate decisions, requirement clarification, project direction\n\n**Async mode** (human unavailable):\n- Write request file to `human-calls/`\n- Use for: offline operations, cross-session pending requests\n\n**First-time bootstrap**: When entering an empty project, the agent SHALL ask the human \"What should this project do?\" via sync human call, then create an openspec change directly from the response. The change proposal captures the human's intent; specs formalize it. No intermediate demands file.\n\n#### Scenario: Sync call — first-time project intent\n- **WHEN** agent enters an empty project\n- **THEN** agent asks the human via sync call, creates an openspec change proposal from the response\n\n#### Scenario: Sync call — immediate decision\n- **WHEN** agent needs a human decision and the human is present\n- **THEN** agent asks directly via conversation\n\n#### Scenario: Async call — offline operation\n- **WHEN** agent needs the human to perform an operation that requires offline time\n- **THEN** agent writes a request to human-calls/, marks dependent tasks as waiting-human\n\n#### Scenario: Human responds to async call\n- **WHEN** a human fills in the Response section of a pending request\n- **THEN** next session processes the response and unblocks dependent work\n\n### Requirement: Non-Blocking Execution\nHuman calls MUST NOT block unrelated tasks.\n\n#### Scenario: Continue after issuing call\n- **WHEN** agent issues a human call and other independent tasks exist\n- **THEN** agent marks dependent tasks as waiting-human and continues other work\n\n### Requirement: Human Call Persistence\nAsync human call requests SHALL be persisted to the file system.\n\nFiles stored in `human-calls/` with filename format `{YYYYMMDD}-{HHmmss}-{short-description}.md`.\n\n#### Scenario: Cross-session persistence\n- **WHEN** session A's human call is unanswered at session end\n- **THEN** the file persists and session B checks for responses on startup\n\n### Requirement: Human Call Types\nThe system SHALL support three types: decision, action, information.\n\n#### Scenario: Decision call\n- **WHEN** agent needs the human to choose between options\n- **THEN** the call lists all options with trade-off analysis\n\n","numLines":58,"startLine":1,"totalLines":58}}}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"tool_kSl4Rox1AMRjrhFEQlHkNzHE","type":"tool_result","content":"     1→\"\"\"SE 3.0 CLI - Main entry point for se3 commands.\"\"\"\n     2→\n     3→import json\n     4→from pathlib import Path\n     5→from typing import Optional\n     6→\n     7→import typer\n     8→\n     9→from . import __version__, SE3_FRAMEWORK_VERSION\n    10→\n    11→def get_framework_version() -> str:\n    12→    \"\"\"Get current framework version from single source of truth (direct file read for git worktree compatibility).\"\"\"\n    13→    import os\n    14→    from pathlib import Path\n    15→    import re\n    16→\n    17→    # Get the path to __init__.py in the current working tree\n    18→    init_file = Path(__file__).parent / \"__init__.py\"\n    19→    if not init_file.exists():\n    20→        raise FileNotFoundError(f\"Cannot find se3_tools __init__.py at {init_file}\")\n    21→\n    22→    with open(init_file, \"r\", encoding=\"utf-8\") as f:\n    23→        content = f.read()\n    24→\n    25→    match = re.search(r'SE3_FRAMEWORK_VERSION\\s*=\\s*\"([\\d]+\\.[\\d]+\\.[\\d]+)\"', content)\n    26→    if not match:\n    27→        raise ValueError(\"Cannot find SE3_FRAMEWORK_VERSION definition in __init__.py\")\n    28→\n    29→    return match.group(1)\n    30→from .commands import lint, status, sync, verify, update, collab, commit, openspec, human_calls_cmd\n    31→from .commands.update import get_installed_se3_version\n    32→from .commands.init import initialize_project\n    33→\n    34→app = typer.Typer(\n    35→    name=\"se3\",\n    36→    help=\"SE 3.0 framework CLI tools\",\n    37→    invoke_without_command=True,\n    38→)\n    39→\n    40→def _version_callback(value: bool):\n    41→    \"\"\"Handle --version flag.\"\"\"\n    42→    if value:\n    43→        typer.echo(f\"se3 CLI version: {__version__}\")\n    44→        typer.echo(f\"SE3 Framework version: {get_framework_version()}\")\n    45→        try:\n    46→            installed = get_installed_se3_version()\n    47→            if installed != \"0.0.0\":\n    48→                typer.echo(f\"Project SE3 version: {installed}\")\n    49→        except Exception:\n    50→            pass\n    51→        raise typer.Exit()\n    52→\n    53→@app.callback()\n    54→def main(\n    55→    ctx: typer.Context,\n    56→    version: bool = typer.Option(\n    57→        False, \"--version\", \"-v\", help=\"Show version information\", callback=_version_callback, is_eager=True\n    58→    ),\n    59→):\n    60→    \"\"\"SE 3.0 framework CLI tools.\"\"\"\n    61→    if ctx.invoked_subcommand is None:\n    62→        typer.echo(ctx.get_help())\n    63→        raise typer.Exit()\n    64→\n    65→\n    66→# Register direct commands\n    67→@app.command(name=\"init\")\n    68→def init_cmd(\n    69→    force: bool = typer.Option(False, \"--force\", \"-f\", help=\"Reinitialize even if already initialized\"),\n    70→    offline: bool = typer.Option(False, \"--offline\", \"-o\", help=\"Use local templates without network\"),\n    71→    with_config: bool = typer.Option(False, \"--with-config\", \"-c\", help=\"Create se3.config.yaml\"),\n    72→    se3_version: str = typer.Option(SE3_FRAMEWORK_VERSION, \"--se3-version\", \"-v\", help=\"Specify SE3 version to use\"),\n    73→):\n    74→    \"\"\"Initialize a new SE 3.0 project.\"\"\"\n    75→    try:\n    76→        initialize_project(force, offline, with_config, se3_version)\n    77→    except Exception as e:\n    78→        typer.echo(\n    79→            typer.style(\n    80→                f\"Error during initialization: {str(e)}\",\n    81→                fg=typer.colors.RED,\n    82→            )\n    83→        )\n    84→        raise typer.Exit(1)\n    85→\n    86→# Register sub-typer commands (complex multi-command tools)\n    87→app.add_typer(lint.app, name=\"lint\", help=\"Lint OpenSpec files\")\n    88→app.add_typer(status.app, name=\"status\", help=\"Check project status\")\n    89→app.add_typer(sync.app, name=\"sync\", help=\"Sync output files\")\n    90→app.add_typer(verify.app, name=\"verify\", help=\"Verify spec coverage\")\n    91→app.add_typer(update.app, name=\"update\", help=\"Update SE 3.0 framework to latest version\")\n    92→app.add_typer(collab.app, name=\"collab\", help=\"Manage git-worktree multi-agent collaboration\")\n    93→app.add_typer(commit.app, name=\"commit\", help=\"Commit changes with SE3 verification\")\n    94→app.add_typer(openspec.app, name=\"openspec\", help=\"Manage OpenSpec directory and specs\")\n    95→app.add_typer(human_calls_cmd.app, name=\"human-calls\", help=\"Manage human calls\")\n    96→\n    97→# Register direct commands (simple single-command tools with positional args)\n    98→# These are registered as direct commands to avoid sub-typer nesting issues\n    99→@app.command(name=\"start\")\n   100→def start_cmd(\n   101→    format: str = typer.Option(\"text\", \"--format\", \"-f\", help=\"Output format (text or json)\"),\n   102→    project_root: str = typer.Option(\".\", \"--project-root\", \"-p\", help=\"Root directory of the project\"),\n   103→):\n   104→    \"\"\"Start an SE3 session — compute state and return actions for the agent.\"\"\"\n   105→    from .commands.start import run_session_start, print_text_report, print_json_report\n   106→    import json\n   107→    state = run_session_start(project_root)\n   108→    if format == \"json\":\n   109→        print_json_report(state)\n   110→    else:\n   111→        print_text_report(state)\n   112→    raise typer.Exit(code=0 if not state.get(\"actions\") else 1)\n   113→\n   114→@app.command(name=\"work\")\n   115→def work_cmd(\n   116→    change_name: Optional[str] = typer.Argument(None, help=\"Name of the change to work on\"),\n   117→    project_root: str = typer.Option(\".\", \"--project-root\", \"-p\", help=\"Root directory of the project\"),\n   118→    new: Optional[str] = typer.Option(None, \"--new\", help=\"Create new change 